{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"840fb2233ebf324b","name":"card_event_depths_of_winter","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Soviet/WinterWar/events/card_event_depths_of_winter","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"DEPTHS OF WINTER","text":"Remove all units from the battlefield. Replace them with LIGHT INFANTRY units.","flavorText":"The ushanka is a traditional Russian fur hat with distinctive ear-flaps that can be folded up and secured atop the hat's crown or fastened beneath the chin, offering protection against cold weather. During the Winter War against Finland, significant organizational failures and inadequate gear exposed many Soviet troops to harsh cold conditions, resulting in fatalities due to exposure. In contrast, the Finnish army possessed superior equipment, notably an ushanka-style fur hat known as the turkislakki M36, which was introduced in 1936. Just prior to the Winter War in 1939, an improved version, the turkislakki M39, was introduced and continues to be in use today. Following the Winter War, the Red Army overhauled its winter uniforms, replacing the Budenovka, a soft woolen hat historically associated with Communist uniforms since the Russian Revolution, with ushankas modeled after the Finnish design. Officers received fur ushankas, while lower-ranking personnel were issued plush or \"fish fur\" ushankas. German soldiers, faced with the severe Russian winter during events like the Battle of Moscow, adopted ushankas and other Soviet-style winter gear because their own uniforms did not adequately shield them from extreme cold conditions.","faction":"Soviet","type":"order","rarity":"Unique","cost":5,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_depths_of_winter","title":{"Namespace":"card_soviet","Key":"card_event_depths_of_winter_title","SourceString":"DEPTHS OF WINTER","LocalizedString":"DEPTHS OF WINTER"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::Soviet","kredit