ing in fatalities due to exposure. In contrast, the Finnish army possessed superior equipment, notably an ushanka-style fur hat known as the turkislakki M36, which was introduced in 1936. Just prior to the Winter War in 1939, an improved version, the turkislakki M39, was introduced and continues to be in use today. Following the Winter War, the Red Army overhauled its winter uniforms, replacing the Budenovka, a soft woolen hat historically associated with Communist uniforms since the Russian Revolution, with ushankas modeled after the Finnish design. Officers received fur ushankas, while lower-ranking personnel were issued plush or \"fish fur\" ushankas. German soldiers, faced with the severe Russian winter during events like the Battle of Moscow, adopted ushankas and other Soviet-style winter gear because their own uniforms did not adequately shield them from extreme cold conditions."},"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Unique","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::WinterWar","isReserved":true,"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/Soviet/CandidateArtwork/Winter_War/t_soviet_winter_order_x.t_soviet_winter_order_x","SubPathString":""},"artist":" Alamy Stock Photo","historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/DEPTHS_OF_WINTER.DEPTHS_OF_WINTER","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoSize":{"X":360.0,"Y":512.0},"historyPhotoDescription":{"Namespace":"card_soviet","Key":"card_event_depths_of_winter_photo","SourceString":"Soviet soldiers wearing ushankas. Ca.1945.","LocalizedString":"Soviet soldiers wearing ushankas. Ca.1945."},"OnPlayedFromHandVisualsSoft":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Blueprints/Effects/BP_Order_DepthsOfWinter.BP_Order_DepthsOfWinter_C","SubPathString":""},"isDirectDamage":true},"variables":[{"name":"bordLeftCardIDs","type":"TArray<int32>","direction":"in"},{"name":"boardRightCardIDs","type":"TArray<int32>","direction":"in"},{"name":"boardFrontlineCardIDs","type":"TArray<int32>","direction":"in"},{"name":"sideOfThisCardHasFrontline","type":"bool"